course: dictionary
lesson: 5072
title: Big words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word institution can mean a large organisation. «The Qing dynasty ruled through Chinese institutions» means the ruling worked through organisations and systems, not through buildings or shops.
explain: Institution can also mean a custom or tradition that has lasted a long time, like Sunday lunch in many families. The Manchus «kept Manchu customs», and those customs were a kind of tradition. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the meaning is a joke. If your town's fish and chip shop has been open for seventy years, people might call it «a local institution». They mean everyone knows it and it has always been there. Read the words around the hard word, and check your meaning fits.
fact: An institution is a large organisation, such as a university, bank, hospital, museum or school.
fact: An institution can also be a custom or tradition that has existed for a long time, such as Sunday lunch.
fact: Long ago, an institution could mean a big building where people were kept and cared for, like an old children's home. This meaning is old and can sound negative.
fact: Informally, a person or place that everyone knows and has been around a long time is «an institution».
fact: Useful phrases: financial institution, educational institution, public institution, a local institution.
exercise: «The Qing dynasty ruled through Chinese institutions.» In this sentence, what is an institution most like? | A gentle breeze | A type of shoe | A very small snack | *An organisation or system that helps run a country
exercise: «We have eaten Sunday lunch together for years. It is a family institution.» What does institution mean here? | A large bank | *A tradition that has lasted a long time | A cold, empty room | A new game
exercise: «The fish and chip shop is a local institution.» Which meaning fits best? | A very tall building | A shop that closed last week | A shop that sells only fish | *A place everyone knows that has been around a long time
test: Which of these is NOT an institution? | A bank | *A puddle in the playground | A museum | A school
test: «The old building was an institution where children were cared for long ago.» What does institution mean here? | A small pet shop | A new kind of sport | *A big building where people were kept and cared for | A happy holiday
exam: Which sentence uses institution as a custom or tradition? | «The museum is an institution full of old coins.» | «The hospital is an institution with many doctors.» | «The bank is an institution in our city.» | *«Our family has an institution of pancakes every Shrove Tuesday.»
